{"name":"Church Mouse","hex":"#b3b5af","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"church mouse","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative form of churchmouse."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/church_mouse"}],"entries":[{"title":"The Church Mouse","blocks":[{"text":"The Church Mouse is a 1934 British comedy film directed by Monty Banks and starring Laura La Plante, Ian Hunter and Edward Chapman. It was made by the British subsidiary of Warner Brothers at the company's Teddington Studios. It was made as a more expensive production than much of the studio's low-budget quota quickie output."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/c2/The_Church_Mouse.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Church_Mouse"},{"title":"The Church Mice series","blocks":[{"text":"The Church Mice series is a series of children's picture books written by English writer Graham Oakley. The books focus on the adventures of a group of church mice who live in an old gothic church in the fictional town of Wortlethorpe, England, and their guardian, Sampson the cat. The books have been widely praised for their richly detailed illustrations and their witty, ironic humor. Several of the church mice books have been nominated for or won major literary awards."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Church_Mice_series"},{"title":"Mouse","blocks":[{"text":"A mouse is a small rodent, characteristically known to have a pointed snout, small rounded ears, a body-length scaly tail, and a high breeding rate. The best known mouse species is the common house mouse. Mice are widely available as pets, but not as popular as some other rodents. In some places, certain kinds of field mice are locally common. They are known to invade homes for food and shelter."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/%D0%9C%D1%8B%D1%88%D1%8C_2.jpg/330px-%D0%9C%D1%8B%D1%88%D1%8C_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mouse"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Fatmouse.jpg/500px-Fatmouse.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Fatmouse.jpg/500px-Fatmouse.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Knockout mouse (left) and normal mouse (right)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFatmouse.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/Fancy_mice.jpg/500px-Fancy_mice.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/Fancy_mice.jpg/1280px-Fancy_mice.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/Fancy_mice.jpg/500px-Fancy_mice.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Pet mice","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFancy_mice.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Feeder_mice.jpg/500px-Feeder_mice.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Feeder_mice.jpg/500px-Feeder_mice.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"\"Pinkie\" mice for sale as reptile feed","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFeeder_mice.jpg"}],"sounds":{},"pictures":[{"title":"Grey bucchero-ware bowl, Clay, 1000-700 BCE, Nr. Babakõy, Turkey, Fitzwilliam Museum, Cambridge","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Grey_bucchero-ware_bowl%2C_Clay%2C_1000-700_BCE%2C_Nr._Babak%C3%B5y%2C_Turkey%2C_Fitzwilliam_Museum%2C_Cambridge.jpg/500px-Grey_bucchero-wa